Right fix in another place, for one defect: a helper in wger/gym/helpers.py
says whether an account is a general manager or a superuser, from the
permission tables, and the view refuses a general manager who targets
one. The gym manager's paths (s3, s4) stay open.

Fixes: s5-reset-password-general-manager

diff --git a/wger/gym/helpers.py b/wger/gym/helpers.py
index 2fa3f30..13ab9fc 100644
--- a/wger/gym/helpers.py
+++ b/wger/gym/helpers.py
@@ -76,6 +76,25 @@ def is_same_gym(user_a, user_b):
     return gym_a is not None and gym_a == gym_b
 
 
+def is_top_account(user):
+    """
+    Whether the account is a superuser or holds manage_gyms, also when it
+    is deactivated
+    """
+    # Django
+    from django.contrib.auth.models import Permission
+    from django.db.models import Q
+
+    return (
+        user.is_superuser
+        or Permission.objects.filter(
+            Q(user=user) | Q(group__user=user),
+            content_type__app_label='gym',
+            codename='manage_gyms',
+        ).exists()
+    )
+
+
